./docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:12842:        "caption": "Figure 1: BIOREASON Architecture. Schematic representation of our novel multimodal framework that integrates a DNA foundation model with a Large Language Model.",
./docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:12859:        "rationale": "Figure 1 validly depicts the route’s input mechanism: DNA sequences are transformed into dense embeddings, projected into Qwen3 space, and stacked with text embeddings before entering the Qwen3 backbone. Under the atlas rules, a shared architecture figure can support named variants from the same paper when the depicted input mechanism is the same, and the exact variant name need not appear. Although the example encoder label in the schematic is Evo2-1B rather than Enformer, the crop still visibly shows the relevant route-specific representation and transformation interface for the Enformer-Qwen3-4B fine-tuning route.",
