./docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:31052:      "no_figure_rationale": "Figure 1 depicts backbones, training stages, and biological modalities, including proteins and ESM3, but it does not visibly show either listed actual-model-input route: (1) ESM-3 residue embeddings projected and inserted at protein placeholder positions, or (2) the structured protein metadata/text prompt supplied as tokens. Under the atlas rules, a valid crop must show the source object, representation, transformation, or immediate interface for at least one supported route. The remaining candidate figures are performance and ablation plots with no input path. There is therefore no defensible crop or replacement figure.",
./docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:31582:        "caption": "Figure 1: Landscape of TeamPath (a) Steps of dataset curation. We extract image-text pairs from a processed TCGA dataset (PathGen-1.6M). (b) Word cloud visualization of ROI captions (upper) and questions (bottom). (c) The core visual language model architecture of TeamPath. (d) TeamPath as a system with an LLM-enhanced router (with over 80% accuracy in choosing the correct approach) and the corresponding capacities in various downstream applications. The logo fire means that we need to adjust the parameters of models, and the logo snowflake means that we do not change the parameters. (e) Overall ranking list of different methods across tasks and metrics. A lower rank (larger bubble) means a better method.",
