./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_135517/docling/document.json:2529:      "orig": "Figure 1. From sequential reading to selective genomic scanning. (a) Sparse, discontinuous genomic signals make sequential modeling inefficient. (b) OCR-inspired genomic modeling enables efficient, reconstructible visual compression. (c) 2D CNNs outperform 1D CNNs in accuracy-efficiency trade-offs on eQTL prediction. (d) Vision tokens substantially reduce the effective token count.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_135517/docling/document.json:2530:      "text": "Figure 1. From sequential reading to selective genomic scanning. (a) Sparse, discontinuous genomic signals make sequential modeling inefficient. (b) OCR-inspired genomic modeling enables efficient, reconstructible visual compression. (c) 2D CNNs outperform 1D CNNs in accuracy-efficiency trade-offs on eQTL prediction. (d) Vision tokens substantially reduce the effective token count."
