./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/subagents/replacement_cropper/model_9ead93555f87/prompt.txt:15:  "adjudicator_rationale": "The current crop is from Figure 6 and shows a perturbation prediction framework, not the virtual screening input route described for primary tumor and cell line profiles. Figure 7 is the correct source-paper figure: its panel A visibly depicts the two relevant input contexts and the C2S screening interface. That is better evidence than adjusting the current Figure 6 crop.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/subagents/replacement_cropper/model_9ead93555f87/prompt.txt:33:      "supporting_figure_or_table": "Figure 7",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/subagents/replacement_cropper/model_9ead93555f87/prompt.txt:67:      "supporting_figure_or_table": "Figure 7",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/subagents/replacement_cropper/model_9ead93555f87/prompt.txt:86:  "figure_caption": "Figure 7: Virtual screening with C2S-Scale nominates a context-dependent modulator of antigen presentation. A, Schematic of the dual-context virtual screening workflow. The model predicts perturbation outcomes on MHC-I antigen presentation gene sets using initial states derived from primary tumor profiles (immune context-positive) and cell line profiles (immune context-neutral). B, Volcano plot displaying predicted drug effects in the primary tumor screen. Silmitasertib (red star) is identified as a high-scoring novel candidate. Inset details the top-ranking compounds, stratified by prior evidence: known MHC-I modulators (dark blue), plausible candidates with pathway links (light blue), and novel hits (grey). C, Experimental validation of the positive control, trametinib. Dose-response assessment of HLA-A,B,C surface levels (Mean Fluorescence Intensity; MFI) in WAGA cells treated with indicated concentrations of trametinib in the absence (gray) or presence (blue) of IFNβ (2 U/ml). D, Predicted context specificity of silmitasertib, showing a significantly higher antigen presentation score in the primary tumor context compared to the cell line context. E, Experimental validation of the novel hit, silmitasertib. Dose-response assessment of MHC-I MFI (normalized to vehicle control) in WAGA cells treated with silmitasertib without (gray) or with (blue) low-dose IFNβ (2 U/ml). Error bars represent mean ± s.d. Significance calculated via two-way t-test with Benjamini-Hochberg correction for multiple comparisons; ∗ P < 0 . 05 , ∗ ∗ P < 0 . 01 , ∗ ∗ ∗ P < 0 . 001 , ∗ ∗ ∗ ∗ P < 0 . 0001 .",
